/-! ## 15. Repair 20: PNT consequences and the finite-condition density limit for A

This section proves more of the remaining glue instead of taking the final
forms of Lemma 3.1 and Lemma 3.2 as primitive fields.

For `A`, the manuscript's actual argument is: impose finitely many gcd
conditions, use periodicity/squarefree tail control to get a density, and then
use the summable tail of omitted conditions to pass uniformly to the infinite
intersection.  We formalize exactly that limiting step below.

